# G050 — Shapes

*v2. See `shapes.md` for prose: polymorphic dispatch on Shape values, first
Rosetta project with method-per-variant dispatch (area, perimeter, name).*

---

## Choreographic Case: Asset Library with Mixed Shape Metadata

[gallery-metadata @canvas-size
    IN ORDER TO
        summarize bounding-region coverage across a mixed-shape asset library
        where each asset's bounding-region may be a circle or a rectangle

    @assets <- [gallery[images]]
    @bounding-shapes <- @assets mapped to :bounding-region

    @total-coverage <- [shape[total-area {shapes: @bounding-shapes}]]
    @densest        <- [shape[largest-by-area {shapes: @bounding-shapes}]]

    where
        every shape is valid
        and total coverage is positive and below @canvas-size
        || -> #metadata-anomaly @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[shape
    area                 {shape}           ;; polymorphic: circle or rectangle
    perimeter            {shape}
    name                 {shape}
    total-area           {shapes}
    largest-by-area      {shapes}
    sort-by-perimeter    {shapes}
    valid                {shape}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: polymorphic dispatch via kind-tag on shape value

A shape is a bare record with a `:kind` discriminator:

{kind: "circle", radius: 10}
{kind: "rectangle", width: 20, height: 30}

[shape[area {shape: @s}]
    where
        when @s:kind is "circle"    the result is π × radius²
        and when @s:kind is "rectangle" the result is width × height
        and when @s:kind is unknown resists with "shape-kind-unknown"
]

The resolver dispatches on `:kind`. Adding a triangle is a resolver
extension — add the case to the `where` and the dispatch in the resolver.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @c <- {kind: "circle", radius: 5}
    @r <- {kind: "rectangle", width: 4, height: 6}

    -> [shape[area       {shape: @c}]]  ;; -> 78.53... (π × 25)
    -> [shape[perimeter  {shape: @c}]]  ;; -> 31.41... (2π × 5)
    -> [shape[area       {shape: @r}]]  ;; -> 24
    -> [shape[perimeter  {shape: @r}]]  ;; -> 20

    -> [shape[total-area {shapes: [@c, @r]}]]         ;; -> 102.53...
    -> [shape[largest-by-area {shapes: [@c, @r]}]]    ;; -> @c (circle is larger)
]
